{
  "_comment": "How children's messages are rewritten before parsing (services/utterance_parser.py, normalize). \"words\" maps a child spelling to the standard one, word by word; \"digit_shorthand\" does the same for shorthand with digits; \"greetings\" turns stretched greetings into the word. \"steps\" run in order: a step with \"pattern\" is a regular expression replaced by \"replace\" (Python's \\\\1 for a group) or \"template\" ({1} for a group, {1|upper}, {1|capitalize}, {1|title} or {1|title_and} to change its case); \"keep_if_group_matches\" leaves a match as it is when the named group matches its pattern, and \"only_if\" runs the step only when the whole message matches; \"word_list\" fills {words} in the pattern with the words, longest first. A step with \"code\" runs a function in the parser. \"examples\" pairs a message with what normalize returns for it; tests/test_normalizations.py checks them.",
